emphasizes the use of electronic musical instruments or electronic music technology as a central aspect of the sound of the music. Historically, electronic music was considered to be any music created with the use of electronic musical instruments or electronic processing, but in modern times, that distinction has been lost because almost all recorded music today, and the majority of live music performances, depend on extensive use of electronics.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "BTS", "streams": 13720, "best_position": 50}, {"artist": "Dua Lipa", "streams": 7614, "best_position": 38}, {"artist": "Lady Gaga", "streams": 7286, "best_position": 48}, {"artist": "KATSEYE", "streams": 5671, "best_position": 81}, {"artist": "Billie Eilish", "streams": 5296, "best_position": 97}, {"artist": "Arctic Monkeys", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Beyonc\u00e9", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Britney Spears", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Carly Rae Jepsen", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Charli xcx", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Cigarettes After Sex", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Ellie Goulding", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "electropop": {"genre": "electropop", "country_code": "hk", "country_name": "Hong Kong", "summary": "Electropop is a type of electronic pop music which features crackly synthesizers prominently in the mix.   Electropop has become an increasingly common term for this music post-2000 whereas in earlier years, synthpop was probably the more common term for pop music using synthesizers.\n\nWhen Kraftwerk first appeared in the mid-1970's, their music was described as electronic body music (ebm) in Germany, Krautrock in England, and technopop in Japan.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "Dua Lipa", "streams": 7614, "best_position": 38}, {"artist": "Lady Gaga", "streams": 7286, "best_position": 48}, {"artist": 